.\" Manpage for webpage2pdf-server.
.TH WEBPAGE2PDF-SERVER 1 "2026-09-07" "webpage2pdf 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
webpage2pdf\-server \- local drag\-and\-drop web front end for webpage2pdf
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B webpage2pdf-server
[\fB\-p\fR \fIPORT\fR] [\fB\-o\fR \fIDIR\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-browser\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Starts a small web app on
.I http://127.0.0.1:8765
and opens it in your browser. Paste links or file paths one per line, or drop
saved
.I .html
files onto the page.
.PP
The server binds to
.I 127.0.0.1
only, so it is not reachable from the network, and it is built on the Python
standard library, so there is no web framework to install. Nothing is uploaded
anywhere; the only outbound traffic is fetching the pages you asked for.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-port " \fIPORT\fR"
Port to listen on. Default: 8765.
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " \fIDIR\fR"
Where finished PDFs are saved. Default:
.IR ~/Documents/webpage2pdf .
.TP
.B \-\-no\-browser
Do not open a browser window on start.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR webpage2pdf (1)
